<title>FINLAND: Stockmann profit rises -agency.</title>
<headline>Stockmann profit rises -agency.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-08-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish retail and department store group Stockmann's first half profit before extraordinary items rose over 50 million markka to 161.7 million markka, Finnish news agency STT reported on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The results were due to be released at 1400/1100 GMT.</p>
<p>Nobody at Stockmann was immediately available for comment.</p>
<p>In the corresponding period last year, Stockmann's profit before extraordinaries was 95.6 million markka.</p>
<p>The first half 1997 earnings included 26.9 million markka in extraordinary gains from the sale of shares in Kesko and MTV, STT said.</p>
<p>Shortly after the agency report was issued, the Helsini bourse suspended trade in Stockmann pending release of the official figures.</p>
<p>-- Helsinki Newsroom +358-9-680 50 242, news@reuters.fi</p>
